{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Brings runtime/<app> in line with the bundle a library ships in data/<lib>/_APPS/<app> - the update twin of materialize_apps, used by dev.git.after_update, dev.dev.install_lib and dev.git.overlay. apps is a JSONArray of app names ([] = every app the library ships). Per app: not in runtime/ yet -> copied whole (installed, NOT activated); already set up -> every shipped file overwrites its counterpart, app.properties included (refreshed). A runtime/<app> that is a SYMLINK (dev.github.import links it when the repo carries runtime/<lib>) is written THROUGH like any other and also listed under through - the checkout behind the link then shows those files as changed when its tracked copy differed from the bundle; only a link that resolves to the bundle itself is left alone (linked), and a link whose target is missing is an error. botd.properties is local state: an existing one is never overwritten or deleted. Files in runtime/<app> that the bundle does not ship are left alone, except those named in removed - a JSONArray of \"<app>/<relative path>\" strings for files an update deleted from the bundle; each is deleted from runtime/<app> only when the bundle really no longer ships it, and emptied directories are pruned. config.properties apps= is never written: activating an app stays the user's act (the app app's Activate button). Returns FLAT {status, lib, installed, refreshed, through, linked, missing (named apps with no bundle), files (files written; identical files are skipped), deleted, errors}.","import":"use ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse ndata::data::Data;\nuse flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse std::fs;\nuse std::path::Path;","params":[{"name":"lib","type":"String"},{"name":"apps","type":"JSONArray"},{"name":"removed","type":"JSONArray"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"ztrojz1a1fa186c0ex1","readers":[],"time":1795225043277,"username":"system","writers":[]}